---
description: Testing
globs: src/**/__tests__/**/*.test.ts
---
* tests will use the `// Arrange` `// Act` `// Assert` comment convention.
* We should have a test for every production class or function. Vitest is the test runner (`npm test`).
* mocks in unit tests will have a suffix of Mock
* spies in unit tests will have a suffix of Spy
* tests will always live in a `__tests__` folder next to the SUTs they test (Vitest only discovers `src/**/__tests__/**/*.test.ts`).
* tests will always be named after the production code's filename, but with the `.test.ts` suffix.
* test suites name sut variable with the keyword `target`
* tests will use random generated data where appropriate from the test-utils files.
* No `any` types
